@startuml
!include style.puml
title SD07 — production load, meaningful mutation and save-failure restoration
participant "App.init / CLIApp.main" as Entry
control EventPlanningFacade as F
participant JsonPlanRepository as R
participant PlanDataMapper as M
participant EventService as S
== Startup ==
Entry -> F : persistent()
F -> R : new JsonPlanRepository(AppDataDirectory.resolve())
note over R : Acquire exclusive OS file lock; reject second owning session
F -> R : load()
note over R : Strict JSON/version checks; absent new blueprint refs default to null
R -> M : restore(data) [semantic validation]
M --> R : validated graph
R --> F : Optional<PlanData>
opt Saved data present
  F -> F : restore(data)
  F -> M : restore(data)
  M --> F : restored events / stable identities
  F -> S : restoreEvents(restored)
  note over F : Restore draft maps and pending changes; subscribe fresh service observers
end
note over Entry,R : Invalid saved data aborts startup; no empty-store reset or automatic overwrite
== Each controller-mediated mutation ==
F -> F : mutate(operation): lock; capture() before
F -> F : operation.get()
alt Operation throws before post-operation capture
  note over F : Exception propagates; finally unlocks. No general operation-failure rollback asserted.
else Operation returns
  F -> F : capture() after
  alt before equals after
    note over F,R : No save (e.g. simulation); return result
  else State differs
    F -> R : save(after)
    note over R : Verify external-change digest; validate DTO graph
    R -> M : restore(after) [semantic validation]
    note over R : Serialize to same-directory temp file; flush
    R -> R : replace(temporary, file)
    alt Save / after-capture failure
      R --> F : RuntimeException [save failure]
      F -> F : restore(before)
      note over F : Restore domain, drafts, pending proposals and observers; throw storage error
    else Save succeeds
      R --> F : completed; expectedDigest updated
      note over F : Return operation result only after persistence
    end
  end
end
note over R
  replace uses ATOMIC_MOVE when supported, normal replacement fallback.
  No backup history, universal power-loss guarantee or network multi-user store.
  close releases file lock; lock-file existence alone is not a live lock.
end note
@enduml
